Description: Allow VA-API H.264 encoders that emit in-band headers (VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_NONE)
 Stateful V4L2 M2M VA-API backends such as qcom-va-driver (Qualcomm Iris)
 generate SPS, PPS, and slice headers in firmware and therefore report
 VAConfigAttribEncPackedHeaders == VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_NONE. They also do
 not implement the stateless VAEncMiscParameterTypeSubMbPartPel hint.
 .
 Accept VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_NONE alongside the full packed-header set,
 pass VA_ENC_PACKED_HEADER_NONE to vaCreateConfig, omit packed header and
 SubMbPartPel misc buffers when the driver emits in-band headers, and reserve
 MAX_HEADER_SIZE in the coded output buffer.
Author: Salami Local Build
Origin: other, local Qualcomm Iris VA-API enablement for GNOME Remote Desktop 50.2
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

